# Project Read-Map

Global doctrine is already loaded from `~/.cursor/rules/profile/`. The documents below
are **not** loaded — `AI_PROFILE/**` and `.cursor/repo-context/**` are never auto-read.
Open them with the Read tool before writing code that touches the listed area.

| Task touches | MUST read first |
|---|---|
| `centos/`, `debian-nft/`, or `debian-ufw/` refresh scripts, or a `dynhosts.json.example` / `zones.json.example` | `.cursor/repo-context/architecture-decisions.md`, `.cursor/repo-context/dangerous-areas.md`, `.cursor/repo-context/known-constraints.md`, `.cursor/repo-context/patterns-and-antipatterns.md`, `AI_PROFILE/languages/shell/style.md`, `AI_PROFILE/languages/shell/patterns.md` |
| README install or operator behavior | `.cursor/repo-context/known-constraints.md`, `.cursor/repo-context/architecture-decisions.md` |

The shell guide is general. Where it conflicts with this repo's constraints (no `set -e`, unquoted nft lines, no lock), the repo-context docs win.

Project docs in `.cursor/repo-context/` outrank portable doctrine on conflict.
